<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $193.6 mln April 1.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $193.6 mln April 1.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $193.6 million surplus on April 1 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON APRIL 1</p>
<p>Exports: $207.6 million</p>
<p>Imports: $176.8 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $333.4 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $170.6 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $193.6 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 2485418))</p>
